{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791028862,"nonce":"7Ci4SjQbwCEtOLdCZy5GbeVf9pg=","title":"Rasterize parsed SVG without usvg, and drop SVG text support from the build","message":"ashui parses SVG in Haxe, then writes it back to markup that blinc_svg parses again with usvg, roxmltree, svgtypes and simplecss. blinc_svg also enables resvg's text and system-font features, which ashui never uses: it rejects SVG \u003ctext\u003e. In the release blinc_abi (3.1 MB), cargo bloat puts about 600 KB of code in that stack: usvg 339 KB, tiny_skia 153 KB, resvg 66 KB, tiny_skia_path 47 KB, svgtypes 45 KB, roxmltree 41 KB, fontdb 33 KB, simplecss 28 KB.\n\nAsked blinc-b1 on 2026-10-03 for (1) a `svg_text` feature, default on, so ashui can depend on blinc_svg without it, and (2) a typed scene rasterizer: groups with opacity and transform, paths of path commands, solid or currentColor paints, rasterized straight with tiny-skia, with the markup parser behind a feature.\n\nWhen they land: build blinc_svg without svg_text or the parser, and pass SvgDocument's nodes to the scene rasterizer instead of SvgWriter's markup. Keep SvgWriter for interning documents by their canonical form.","files":null}]}